这让我联想到了。

1219
00:57:20.910 --> 00:57:22.570
It all came full circle in your brain.
你脑子里的一切都串联起来了。

1220
00:57:22.590 --> 00:57:23.610
And you need to see it.
你一定要看看。

1221
00:57:23.690 --> 00:57:25.190
You love survivalist stuff.
你很喜欢生存类节目吧。

1222
00:57:25.330 --> 00:57:25.750
I do.
我是挺喜欢的。

1223
00:57:25.750 --> 00:57:35.390
OK, now we have to get into the very, very awkward scene that is Karen and Pam in the kitchen.
好了，现在我们得聊聊厨房里凯伦和帕姆那场非常、非常尴尬的戏。

1224
00:57:35.730 --> 00:57:37.950
They're kind of joking about Ben Franklin.
她们当时在拿本·富兰克林开玩笑。

1225
00:57:38.470 --> 00:57:43.230
I feel like they're both like doing a bit about how did he become a Ben Franklin impersonator.
我觉得她们俩都在演，讨论他是怎么成为本·富兰克林模仿者的。

1226
00:57:43.390 --> 00:57:54.530
And all of a sudden, Karen takes a sharp left turn and she says, hey, you know, I just want you to know Jim told me, you know, that you guys kissed.
突然间，凯伦话锋一转，她说，嘿，你知道吗，我只是想让你知道，吉姆告诉我，你们接过吻。

1227
00:57:56.590 --> 00:57:59.690
And, you know, and Pam's like, what the what?
然后，帕姆当时就懵了。

1228
00:58:00.950 --> 00:58:03.750
She is she's like, what is happening right now?
她当时心想，这到底是怎么回事？

1229
00:58:03.970 --> 00:58:05.370
It's like her computer shut down.
就像她的电脑死机了一样。

1230
00:58:06.290 --> 00:58:06.770
Yes.
没错。

1231
00:58:07.230 --> 00:58:11.190
Now, pretty much none of what she says after this makes any sense.
现在，她在这之后说的几乎所有话都毫无逻辑。

1232
00:58:12.310 --> 00:58:12.790
No.
确实。

1233
00:58:13.050 --> 00:58:15.130
And OK, so we had someone write in.
好的，有位观众来信问。

1234
00:58:15.310 --> 00:58:17.490
Jackie Cortez said when Pam answers.
杰基·科尔特斯问，当帕姆回答时。

1235
00:58:18.170 --> 00:58:18.990
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

1236
00:58:19.330 --> 00:58:20.190
To Karen.
对凯伦说。

1237
00:58:20.450 --> 00:58:22.610
When Karen asked if she still has feelings for Jim.
当凯伦问她是否还对吉姆有感情时。

1238
00:58:23.090 --> 00:58:30.030
Do you think that was because Pam was feeling brave in the moment that she was like trying to say her real feelings in that moment?
你觉得那是因为帕姆当时感觉很勇敢，所以试图说出自己的真实感受吗？

1239
00:58:30.030 --> 00:58:32.370
And then she backs out when she sees Karen's face.
然后当她看到凯伦的表情时又退缩了。

1240
00:58:32.530 --> 00:58:37.810
And also how much of this was scripted and how much of it was improvised?
另外，这场戏有多少是剧本写的，有多少是即兴发挥的？

1241
00:58:38.970 --> 00:58:44.150
OK, so first of all, this scene plays out exactly as it was scripted.
好的，首先，这场戏完全是按照剧本演的。

1242
00:58:44.810 --> 00:58:49.870
All of those like awkward jumps in dialogue were all scripted.
所有那些尴尬的对话跳跃都是剧本写好的。

1243
00:58:50.150 --> 00:58:52.850
I just think it is such a great piece of writing.
我觉得这剧本写得太棒了。

1244
00:58:52.850 --> 00:59:00.490
And I remember I felt being challenged as an actor to make all those different turns that Pam has to make in the scene.
我记得当时作为演员，我感到很有挑战性，要表现出帕姆在这一幕中所有的情绪转折。

1245
00:59:00.490 --> 00:59:07.050
And so when she says, oh, yeah, that's because she heard the question.
所以当她说“哦，是啊”时，那是因为她听到了问题。

1246
00:59:07.050 --> 00:59:09.050
You don't have feelings for Jim.
你对吉姆没有感情了。

1247
00:59:09.250 --> 00:59:09.390
Right.
对。

1248
00:59:09.670 --> 00:59:12.530
And she's like, oh, yeah, I don't have feelings.
然后她说，哦，是啊，我没有感情了。

1249
00:59:12.730 --> 00:59:14.090
But that's not what Karen said.
但凯伦问的不是这个。

1250
00:59:14.290 --> 00:59:17.210
Karen said, you do you still have feelings for Jim?
凯伦问的是，你是不是还对吉姆有感情？

1251
00:59:17.410 --> 00:59:18.590
And she's like, oh, yeah.
然后她就说，哦，是啊。

1252
00:59:19.470 --> 00:59:22.370
But like Pam is just like she's not hearing everything.
但帕姆就像是没听全所有内容一样。

1253
00:59:22.370 --> 00:59:29.010
And she's just like her mind is being blown right now by the fact that Jim told Karen this.
她现在整个人都惊呆了，因为吉姆竟然把这件事告诉了凯伦。

1254
00:59:29.370 --> 00:59:29.490
Yeah.
没错。

1255
00:59:29.490 --> 00:59:31.070
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

1256
00:59:31.170 --> 00:59:33.110
Because now it's everything we were talking about.
因为现在这成了我们刚才讨论的一切。

1257
00:59:33.450 --> 00:59:35.110
It's not a secret anymore.
这不再是什么秘密了。

1258
00:59:35.330 --> 00:59:37.550
It's not Jim and Pam's secret anymore.
这不再是吉姆和帕姆之间的秘密了。

1259
00:59:37.870 --> 00:59:44.850
That I think tells Pam that he's taking this relationship with Karen seriously because he's willing to tell her the real truth.
我觉得这告诉帕姆，他是在认真对待和凯伦的关系，因为他愿意告诉她真相。

1260
00:59:45.090 --> 00:59:49.890
And now I think Pam is just in like a deer in headlights kind of mode.
现在我觉得帕姆就像一只被车灯惊住的鹿一样，不知所措。

1261
00:59:50.070 --> 00:59:51.290
Well, I thought it was fantastic.
嗯，我觉得这太棒了。

1262
00:59:51.290 --> 00:59:53.870
I thought you the two of you did such a great job with it.
我觉得你们俩演得太好了。

1263
00:59:53.870 --> 00:59:56.450
It was written so well and acted so well.
剧本写得好，演得也很好。

1264
00:59:56.610 --> 00:59:59.110
And, oh, it made me so uncomfortable.
而且，噢，这让我感到非常不自在。

1265
00:59:59.170 --> 01:00:00.830
So you guys know you did the right.
所以你们知道你们做对了。

1266
01:00:01.050 --> 01:00:02.130
You did your job.
你们完成了自己的工作。

1267
01:00:03.270 --> 01:00:05.290
Rashida and I had a lot of fun shooting that scene.
拉什达和我拍那场戏时玩得很开心。

1268
01:00:05.670 --> 01:00:05.930
All right.
好的。

1269
01:00:06.050 --> 01:00:12.590
Should we go back down to the warehouse where Kevin is leading all of the guys in a card game?
我们要回到仓库吗？凯文正在那里带着大家玩牌。

1270
01:00:12.590 --> 01:00:12.770
Yeah.
好啊。

1271
01:00:12.890 --> 01:00:18.270
He says it's a no limit deuce to seven low ball, which I think is the same one he did in Casino Night, right?
他说这是无限注二七低牌，我觉得这和他在“赌场之夜”里玩的是同一种，对吧？

1272
01:00:19.490 --> 01:00:19.930
Yes.
是的。

1273
01:00:20.050 --> 01:00:23.310
That is what he won in the World Series of Poker.
那就是他在世界扑克系列赛中赢的那种。

1274
01:00:23.310 --> 01:00:23.490
Okay.
好的。

1275
01:00:23.590 --> 01:00:25.650
He tells us in Casino Night.
他在“赌场之夜”里告诉过我们。

1276
01:00:25.650 --> 01:00:28.310
And then Michael shuffles the cards like a total idiot.
然后迈克尔洗牌的样子简直像个彻头彻尾的白痴。

1277
01:00:29.630 --> 01:00:30.150
Yes.
没错。

1278
01:00:30.550 --> 01:00:31.070
Yes.
是的。

1279
01:00:31.190 --> 01:00:38.510
We had a fan catch from Katie who said in this episode around 12 minutes, 46 seconds, Kevin's wearing glasses again.
我们收到了一位粉丝凯蒂的发现，她说在这一集的12分46秒左右，凯文又戴上眼镜了。

1280
01:00:38.870 --> 01:00:39.750
There he is.
他就在那儿。

1281
01:00:39.870 --> 01:00:43.030
He wears glasses when he plays poker, but not when he's working.
他打扑克时戴眼镜，但工作时不戴。

1282
01:00:43.230 --> 01:00:45.470
Not as an accountant, just when he plays cards.
当会计时不戴，只有打牌时才戴。

1283
01:00:45.710 --> 01:00:48.150
And this is when Elizabeth enters.
这时伊丽莎白进来了。

1284
01:00:48.250 --> 01:00:50.050
She comes out of Daryl's office.
她从达里尔的办公室走出来。

1285
01:00:50.050 --> 01:01:00.370
She has changed out of her sweatpants and sweatshirt, and she is now in a breakaway, sexy office attire.
她换掉了运动裤和运动衫，现在穿的是一套可撕开的性感办公装。

1286
01:01:00.770 --> 01:01:04.130
We had a huge fan catch from Kristen Trogel.
我们收到了克里斯汀·特罗格尔的一个重大发现。

1287
01:01:04.350 --> 01:01:06.010
Kristen, what'd you catch?
克里斯汀，你发现了什么？

1288
01:01:06.430 --> 01:01:13.370
Pam's shirt in the dundies is the same shirt that Elizabeth the stripper rips off in Ben Franklin.
帕姆在“邓迪奖”颁奖礼上穿的衬衫，和脱衣舞娘伊丽莎白在“本·富兰克林”那一集中撕掉的是同一件。

1289
01:01:13.530 --> 01:01:14.590
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1290
01:01:14.590 --> 01:01:16.730
Did they recycle one of your shirts?
他们回收了你的一件衬衫吗？

1291
01:01:16.730 --> 01:01:20.510
Did wardrobe make it like a breakaway kind of blouse or something?
服装组把它改成了那种可以撕开的衬衫吗？

1292
01:01:21.770 --> 01:01:22.290
Yes.
是的。

1293
01:01:22.970 --> 01:01:23.570
Yes.
没错。

1294
01:01:23.850 --> 01:01:26.970
Elizabeth is wearing one of my old shirts.
伊丽莎白穿的是我的一件旧衬衫。

1295
01:01:27.490 --> 01:01:30.770
So I actually first wore it for basketball.
我其实是在拍“篮球”那一集时第一次穿它的。

1296
01:01:31.370 --> 01:01:33.670
And then I wear it again in dundies.
然后我在“邓迪奖”里又穿了一次。

1297
01:01:33.730 --> 01:01:37.950
And I reached out to Carrie Bennett, our wardrobe supervisor, about this.
我为此联系了我们的服装主管嘉莉·贝内特。

1298
01:01:38.090 --> 01:01:38.570
What'd she say?
她怎么说？

1299
01:01:39.830 --> 01:01:42.670
She said that this was not in the script.
她说剧本里并没有写这个。

1300
01:01:42.870 --> 01:01:46.190
This was not like any kind of direction she was given.
她并没有接到任何相关的指示。

1301
01:01:46.410 --> 01:01:50.330
Because a lot of people did write in and ask, like, was this on purpose?
因为很多人写信来问，比如，这是故意的吗？

1302
01:01:50.610 --> 01:01:56.070
Did you want us to notice that this was the identical shirt that Pam has worn?
你们是想让我们注意到这和帕姆穿过的是同一件衬衫吗？

1303
01:01:56.070 --> 01:01:58.210
Was that a joke that was written in the script?
那是剧本里写好的笑话吗？

1304
01:01:58.430 --> 01:01:59.250
It wasn't.
并不是。

1305
01:01:59.510 --> 01:02:07.710
She said that oftentimes when a guest actor is cast at the very last minute, she doesn't have time to go shopping for them.
她说通常当客串演员在最后一刻才定下来时，她没有时间去为他们购物。

1306
01:02:07.710 --> 01:02:13.870
So what wardrobe designers do is they go into their, quote-unquote, retired wardrobe.
所以服装设计师的做法是去翻他们的所谓“退役”服装库。

1307
01:02:14.370 --> 01:02:21.790
And this is a stash of outfits that have been retired, but that used to belong to the main cast members.
这是一堆已经退役，但曾经属于主要演员的服装。

1308
01:02:22.750 --> 01:02:28.910
So she had to find a shirt that fit Elizabeth, and then it had to be converted into a ripaway shirt.
所以她必须找到一件适合伊丽莎白的衬衫，然后还得把它改成一件可以撕开的衬衫。

1309
01:02:29.530 --> 01:02:41.550
And so they just didn't have time to go shopping and convert a shirt into a ripaway shirt because the timing of when Jackie was cast, they had to just go into Pam's old wardrobe.
他们实在没时间去买衣服再改成撕开式衬衫，因为杰基定下来的时间太紧了，他们只能去翻帕姆的旧衣服。

1310
01:02:41.550 --> 01:02:42.610
And that's what they did.
他们就是这么做的。

1311
01:02:42.610 --> 01:02:44.670
And she said she can't believe that people noticed.
她说她真不敢相信竟然有人注意到了。

1312
01:02:45.170 --> 01:02:51.570
Well, listen, Elizabeth, the stripper, you're lucky you didn't get any of Angela Martin's retired wardrobe.
听着，伊丽莎白，那个脱衣舞娘，你很幸运没穿到安吉拉·马丁的退役服装。

1313
01:02:52.290 --> 01:02:53.150
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1314
01:02:53.930 --> 01:02:54.830
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1315
01:02:55.130 --> 01:02:56.430
That would have been very bad.
那可就太糟糕了。

1316
01:02:56.730 --> 01:02:58.510
That's a great catch, though.
不过这真是个了不起的发现。

1317
01:02:59.630 --> 01:03:00.190
I know.
我知道。

1318
01:03:00.370 --> 01:03:03.930
And Carrie also said that this happens all the time on TV shows.
凯莉还说这种情况在电视剧里经常发生。

1319
01:03:04.430 --> 01:03:09.890
She said you will often spot retired clothing from the main cast being repurposed for guest actors.
她说你经常会发现主要演员的退役服装被重新用在客串演员身上。

1320
01:03:10.170 --> 01:03:14.990
I feel like everybody, you can look for that along with the fakie bag.
我觉得大家可以去留意一下，还有那个假包。

1321
01:03:15.250 --> 01:03:15.630
Fakie bag.
假包。

1322
01:03:15.630 --> 01:03:17.990
Well, now she starts her dance.
好了，现在她开始跳舞了。

1323
01:03:18.490 --> 01:03:19.930
It's to bad companies.
那是《Bad Companies》。

1324
01:03:19.950 --> 01:03:21.350
Feel like making love.
《Feel Like Makin' Love》。

1325
01:03:22.550 --> 01:03:24.510
No one wanted the dance.
没人想要这段舞。

1326
01:03:24.730 --> 01:03:25.750
Bob Vance didn't want it.
鲍勃·万斯也不想要。

1327
01:03:25.870 --> 01:03:26.710
Michael's like, OK.
迈克尔心想，好吧。

1328
01:03:27.770 --> 01:03:30.150
And this is so awkward.
这太尴尬了。

1329
01:03:30.450 --> 01:03:32.110
He doesn't know what to do with himself.
他不知道该怎么办才好。

1330
01:03:32.110 --> 01:03:32.950
He's so uncomfortable.
他感到非常不自在。

1331
01:03:33.270 --> 01:03:35.650
He just starts muttering, you smell like Tide.
他只是开始嘟囔，你闻起来像汰渍洗衣液的味道。

1332
01:03:36.150 --> 01:03:36.310
Yep.
没错。

1333
01:03:36.530 --> 01:03:37.030
Smell like Tide.
闻起来像汰渍。

1334
01:03:37.110 --> 01:03:37.790
Do you use Tide?
你用汰渍吗？

1335
01:03:37.930 --> 01:03:39.770
We had a couple of people write in.
我们收到了几位观众的来信。

1336
01:03:39.770 --> 01:03:46.310
And Zuyi and Dan asked, when Elizabeth is dancing on Michael, how much of the dialogue was scripted?
祖伊和丹问，当伊丽莎白在迈克尔身上跳舞时，有多少对话是照着剧本演的？

1337
01:03:47.010 --> 01:03:47.870
All of it.
全部都是。

1338
01:03:48.010 --> 01:03:54.770
And you guys, we've talked a little bit about, like, scenes where someone has to slap someone, you know?
伙计们，我们之前聊过一些场景，比如有人需要扇别人耳光，你们懂的？

1339
01:03:54.930 --> 01:03:57.530
And how we bring in a stunt coordinator.
以及我们是如何请来特技协调员的。

1340
01:03:57.930 --> 01:04:00.330
You do that kind of stuff in scenes like this, too.
像这样的场景，你们也会做同样的事情。

1341
01:04:00.570 --> 01:04:08.690
Any scenes that have any kind of, like, touching, dancing up on someone, a sex scene, they are choreographed.
任何涉及触碰、贴身热舞、性爱场面的戏，都是编排好的。

1342
01:04:09.210 --> 01:04:11.610
Yeah, it's really no different than, like, a fight scene.
没错，这和打斗戏其实没什么区别。

1343
01:04:11.730 --> 01:04:12.670
It's like, I'm going to sit here.
就像是，我要坐在这里。

1344
01:04:12.750 --> 01:04:13.830
I'm going to put my arm here.
我要把胳膊放在这儿。

1345
01:04:14.110 --> 01:04:15.530
Then I'm going to stand here.
然后我要站在这里。

1346
01:04:16.070 --> 01:04:17.410
It's all rehearsed.
这一切都是排练过的。

1347
01:04:17.570 --> 01:04:18.670
You don't freestyle this stuff.
这种戏是不能即兴发挥的。

1348
01:04:19.110 --> 01:04:19.510
Yeah.
没错。

1349
01:04:19.710 --> 01:04:27.170
So where she sits on his leg, all of the dancing she's going to do, when she's going to rip open her shirt, very scripted.
所以她坐在他腿上的位置，她要跳的所有舞步，她什么时候撕开衬衫，都是严格按照剧本来的。

1350
01:04:27.330 --> 01:04:28.690
The dialogue was scripted.
对话也是写在剧本里的。

1351
01:04:28.850 --> 01:04:37.230
I wasn't surprised when I went back to the script because I thought, yeah, I don't think in a moment like this that they would have, like, freestyled that.
当我回头看剧本时，我一点也不惊讶，因为我想，没错，我觉得在这种时刻，他们是不可能即兴发挥的。

1352
01:04:37.230 --> 01:04:38.790
No, that was all scripted.
不，那全是写好的剧本。

1353
01:04:39.750 --> 01:04:42.170
And Michael is just overwhelmed.
迈克尔当时完全不知所措。

1354
01:04:42.390 --> 01:04:43.210
He's like, this is wrong.
他觉得，这不对劲。

1355
01:04:43.210 --> 01:04:44.030
I have a girlfriend.
我有女朋友了。

1356
01:04:44.030 --> 01:04:46.050
And he storms off.
然后他气冲冲地走了。

1357
01:04:46.210 --> 01:04:47.810
It was just all too much for him.
这一切对他来说实在太沉重了。

1358
01:04:48.190 --> 01:04:54.110
And Dwight, being the frugal fella he is, is like, hey, I paid you for three hours.
而德怀特，作为一个精打细算的家伙，心想，嘿，我付了你三个小时的钱。

1359
01:04:54.930 --> 01:04:56.550
I'm going to get three hours of work out of you.
我就要让你干满三个小时的活。

1360
01:04:56.650 --> 01:04:58.150
So now you have to go answer phones.
所以现在你得去接电话。

1361
01:04:58.150 --> 01:05:03.670
And because Oscar is nowhere to be seen, even though he has returned.
而且因为奥斯卡不见踪影，尽管他已经回来了。

1362
01:05:03.850 --> 01:05:06.070
Did we shoot this out of order, Jenna?
珍娜，我们是乱序拍摄的吗？

1363
01:05:06.330 --> 01:05:07.510
Why isn't Oscar there?
为什么奥斯卡不在那儿？

1364
01:05:07.850 --> 01:05:08.630
I don't know.
我不知道。

1365
01:05:08.630 --> 01:05:12.050
Because the traveling salesman and the return were shot in October.
因为《旅行推销员》和《回归》是在十月份拍摄的。

1366
01:05:12.330 --> 01:05:12.610
Yeah.
没错。

1367
01:05:12.910 --> 01:05:14.290
And this was shot in January.
而这一集是在一月份拍摄的。

1368
01:05:14.290 --> 01:05:17.870
So it doesn't make sense why Oscar isn't there.
所以奥斯卡不在那儿确实说不通。

1369
01:05:18.090 --> 01:05:18.270
It doesn't.
确实说不通。

1370
01:05:18.430 --> 01:05:23.050
So anyway, Dwight brings Elizabeth to accounting to sit in Oscar's seat.
总之，德怀特把伊丽莎白带到会计部，让她坐在奥斯卡的位子上。

1371
01:05:23.390 --> 01:05:25.750
Elizabeth is very overwhelming for Angela.
伊丽莎白让安吉拉感到非常难以招架。

1372
01:05:25.750 --> 01:05:32.130
And she's like, like, sort of like this very Elizabethan, like, fanning myself.
她就像是那种非常伊丽莎白时代风格的人，不停地给自己扇风。

1373
01:05:32.850 --> 01:05:34.390
Well, here's the thing.
嗯，问题是这样的。

1374
01:05:34.510 --> 01:05:36.750
She compliments your baby poster.
她夸奖了你的婴儿海报。

1375
01:05:37.530 --> 01:05:38.650
It doesn't matter.
那不重要。

1376
01:05:38.830 --> 01:05:39.710
It doesn't matter.
那不重要。

1377
01:05:39.810 --> 01:05:40.210
I know.
我知道。

1378
01:05:40.410 --> 01:05:41.630
She really is.
她确实是。

1379
01:05:41.750 --> 01:05:44.770
She's a fan of baby jazz, like your character is.
她和你这个角色一样，也是婴儿爵士乐的粉丝。

1380
01:05:45.290 --> 01:05:47.170
But a lot of people wrote in.
但很多人写信来问。

1381
01:05:47.710 --> 01:05:53.310
Sierra, Tiffany, Camille, and Krista are like, what is the baby poster doing back up?
塞拉、蒂芙尼、卡米尔和克里斯塔都在问，那张婴儿海报怎么又挂回去了？

1382
01:05:54.850 --> 01:05:58.750
Angela, did your character put it up when Oscar went on his sabbatical?
安吉拉，是你的角色在奥斯卡休假时把它挂回去的吗？

1383
01:05:58.910 --> 01:05:59.950
That's what they want to know.
这就是他们想知道的。

1384
01:06:00.150 --> 01:06:01.170
I love this theory.
我喜欢这个理论。

1385
01:06:01.170 --> 01:06:02.550
I fully support it.
我完全支持。

1386
01:06:02.850 --> 01:06:06.570
The minute Oscar left, she's like, my poster is going back up.
奥斯卡一走，她就想，我的海报要挂回去了。

1387
01:06:06.950 --> 01:06:08.830
Meanwhile, Ben Franklin, a.k.a.
与此同时，本·富兰克林，也就是戈登，正在前台搭讪帕姆。

1388
01:06:08.950 --> 01:06:11.210
Gordon, is hitting on Pam at reception.
他在音频片段里也稍微提到了这一点。

1389
01:06:11.790 --> 01:06:14.970
And he said a little bit about this in his audio clip.
哦，哦，太搞笑了。

1390
01:06:15.550 --> 01:06:18.130
Oh, oh, so funny.
太搞笑了。

1391
01:06:18.370 --> 01:06:19.010
So funny.
太搞笑了。

1392
01:06:19.150 --> 01:06:20.970
And now Michael doesn't know what to do.
现在迈克尔不知道该怎么办了。

1393
01:06:21.110 --> 01:06:22.730
He feels like he's cheated on Jan.
他觉得自己背叛了简。

1394
01:06:23.030 --> 01:06:26.010
He talks to Ben Franklin, wants Ben Franklin's advice.
他找本·富兰克林谈话，想要听听他的建议。

1395
01:06:26.510 --> 01:06:30.630
Ben Franklin slash Gordon basically says, I don't think she needs to know this information.
本·富兰克林也就是戈登，基本上说，我觉得她没必要知道这些信息。

1396
01:06:30.630 --> 01:06:34.730
And Michael is like, Ben Franklin, you're kind of a sleazebag.
迈克尔就说，本·富兰克林，你真是个卑鄙小人。

1397
01:06:35.030 --> 01:06:38.650
And you guys, Ben Franklin was kind of a sleazebag with women.
伙计们，本·富兰克林在对待女性方面确实有点卑鄙。

1398
01:06:38.910 --> 01:06:40.370
He like actually really was.
他实际上真的是那样。

1399
01:06:40.530 --> 01:06:47.470
If you look it up, he just he like literally slept with so many women.
如果你去查一下，他真的和很多女性发生过关系。

1400
01:06:47.470 --> 01:06:51.110
And there's one thing that's inaccurate in this episode, though.
不过，这一集里有一件事是不准确的。

1401
01:06:51.390 --> 01:06:56.450
In this episode, you know, he had a child with one woman who was not his wife.
在这一集中，你知道，他和一位非妻子的女性生了一个孩子。

1402
01:06:56.830 --> 01:07:02.330
And in the episode, he says that, like, she didn't know.
而在这一集里，他说，呃，她当时并不知道。

1403
01:07:03.210 --> 01:07:09.810
That he had he sort of says to Michael, like, I fathered a child and I never told my wife about it.
他有点像是对迈克尔说，我有了个私生子，但我从来没告诉过我妻子。

1404
01:07:09.890 --> 01:07:11.230
But that's not true.
但那不是真的。

1405
01:07:11.510 --> 01:07:14.690
Actually, his wife raised that child like her own.
事实上，他的妻子把那个孩子视如己出。

1406
01:07:14.690 --> 01:07:15.870
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1407
01:07:16.450 --> 01:07:19.910
His wife, Deborah, was a saint, I'm going to say.
我想说，他的妻子黛博拉简直是个圣人。

1408
01:07:19.910 --> 01:07:22.330
And she put up with Ben's bad behavior.
她忍受了本的所有恶劣行径。

1409
01:07:22.330 --> 01:07:27.550
Well, now Michael did not like his advice from Ben Franklin.
好吧，迈克尔并不喜欢本·富兰克林给他的建议。

1410
01:07:27.550 --> 01:07:31.230
So he's going to go ask Elizabeth for her advice instead.
所以他打算去问伊丽莎白，听听她的建议。

1411
01:07:31.610 --> 01:07:33.150
Here is her advice to Michael.
这是她给迈克尔的建议。

1412
01:07:33.430 --> 01:07:37.210
Quote, secrets, secrets are no fun.
引用如下：秘密，秘密没意思。

1413
01:07:38.290 --> 01:07:40.850
Secrets, secrets hurt someone.
秘密，秘密会伤人。

1414
01:07:43.260 --> 01:07:44.720
Angela, do you know what that is?
安吉拉，你知道那是什么吗？

1415
01:07:44.860 --> 01:07:45.600
Do you know what that quote is?
你知道那句引语出自哪里吗？

1416
01:07:45.780 --> 01:07:48.560
Please tell me you researched this quote.
请告诉我你查过这句引语。

1417
01:07:48.680 --> 01:07:50.120
Is it from like a children's book?
它是出自什么儿童读物吗？

1418
01:07:50.280 --> 01:07:50.860
What is it from?
它到底出自哪里？

1419
01:07:50.860 --> 01:08:01.700
These are the opening lyrics to a song called No Secrets by a girl band called No Secrets from their album.
这是女子组合“No Secrets”在她们同名专辑中一首名为《No Secrets》的歌的开场歌词。

1420
01:08:01.700 --> 01:08:02.260
No Secrets?
《No Secrets》？

1421
01:08:02.380 --> 01:08:03.320
No Secrets.
《No Secrets》。

1422
01:08:04.300 --> 01:08:06.860
And I asked Sam and Cody to pull a clip.
我让萨姆和科迪找了一段音频剪辑。

1423
01:08:07.000 --> 01:08:07.580
Here it is, Angela.
就在这儿，安吉拉。

1424
01:08:09.420 --> 01:08:13.840
Secrets, secrets are no fun.
秘密，秘密没意思。

1425
01:08:15.780 --> 01:08:19.500
Secrets, secrets hurt someone.
秘密，秘密会伤人。

1426
01:08:33.960 --> 01:08:37.140
No Secrets was a British-American girl band.
“No Secrets”是一个英美女子组合。

1427
01:08:37.140 --> 01:08:38.980
Very reminiscent of Spice Girls.
非常有辣妹组合的感觉。

1428
01:08:39.280 --> 01:08:45.100
They had one hit, which was a cover of Kids in America, that song by Kim Wilde.
她们有一首热门单曲，是翻唱金·怀尔德的那首《Kids in America》。

1429
01:08:45.460 --> 01:08:47.260
We're the kids in America.
我们是美国的年轻人。

1430
01:08:47.600 --> 01:08:49.780
Oh, we're the kids in America.
哦，我们是美国的年轻人。

1431
01:08:50.080 --> 01:08:50.860
Do you remember that song?
你还记得那首歌吗？

1432
01:08:50.960 --> 01:08:51.600
I kind of do.
我有点印象。

1433
01:08:51.840 --> 01:08:57.100
They followed up with another hit single, That's What Girls Do, but they only ever made one album.
她们随后又出了一首热门单曲《That's What Girls Do》，但她们总共只出过一张专辑。

1434
01:08:57.940 --> 01:09:00.640
They started on a second one, but it was never released.
她们开始制作第二张，但从未发行。

1435
01:09:00.640 --> 01:09:06.700
The band broke up over disagreements, and one member claims it was parent drama and interference.
乐队因为分歧而解散，其中一名成员声称是因为家长的闹剧和干预。

1436
01:09:07.260 --> 01:09:09.260
But I, here's the thing.
但我，重点是。

1437
01:09:09.640 --> 01:09:11.920
Mindy Kaling wrote this episode.
敏迪·卡灵写了这一集。

1438
01:09:12.480 --> 01:09:21.500
I have no doubt, no doubt in my mind that she has the album No Secrets by No Secrets, and that's how she knew to quote this line.
我毫不怀疑，我敢肯定她有“No Secrets”组合的《No Secrets》专辑，这就是她知道引用这句歌词的原因。

1439
01:09:21.500 --> 01:09:23.240
I mean, it seems pretty specific.
我是说，这看起来非常具体。

1440
01:09:23.600 --> 01:09:33.820
We also had a fan catch in this scene from Corinna Liu, who says at 17 minutes, 52 seconds, there is a flyer on the refrigerator behind Michael for silver on spruce.
我们还有一位粉丝科琳娜·刘在这一幕中发现了一个细节，她说在17分52秒时，迈克尔身后的冰箱上有一张“Silver on Spruce”的传单。

1441
01:09:34.260 --> 01:09:42.440
Corinna says, I did a small deep dive, and it looks like this is a real business with two different addresses, and the telephone number on the flyer is correct.
科琳娜说，我做了一点深入调查，看起来这是一家真实存在的企业，有两个不同的地址，而且传单上的电话号码也是正确的。

1442
01:09:43.540 --> 01:09:44.800
I checked it out.
我核实过了。

1443
01:09:45.020 --> 01:09:46.060
Corinna is right.
科琳娜是对的。

1444
01:09:46.520 --> 01:09:48.080
Yes, silver on spruce.
没错，Silver on Spruce。

1445
01:09:48.320 --> 01:09:54.240
I wonder if this jewelry store has gotten, like, prank calls because you can see the phone number in our episode.
我不知道这家珠宝店有没有接到过恶作剧电话，因为在我们的剧集里能看到那个电话号码。

1446
01:09:55.140 --> 01:09:58.400
Well, I imagine Corinna is not the first person to freeze frame on this.
嗯，我想科琳娜应该不是第一个对此定格画面的人。

1447
01:09:58.400 --> 01:10:01.300
I wonder if the kids on the talk have called the number.
我在想TikTok上的那些孩子们有没有打过那个电话。

1448
01:10:01.640 --> 01:10:05.600
Lady, it is not called the talk, and you're not going to get them to call at the talk.
大姐，那不叫“the talk”，而且你也不可能让他们去打“the talk”。

1449
01:10:06.360 --> 01:10:06.840
Okay?
好吗？

1450
01:10:07.160 --> 01:10:08.940
Gosh, everyone on the talk.
天哪，TikTok上的每个人。

1451
01:10:09.700 --> 01:10:14.680
All right, guys, we're almost done, I promise, I promise,
好了，各位，我们快讲完了，我保证，我保证，

1452
01:10:14.700 --> 01:10:30.860
but we cannot leave this episode without talking about this scene where Dwight is interrogating Ben Franklin because Jim has convinced him that this is the real Ben Franklin who has time-traveled to visit us at Dunder Mifflin.
但我们不能跳过这一集，必须聊聊德怀特审问本·富兰克林的那个场景，因为吉姆让他相信这就是穿越时空来到邓德·米夫林看望我们的真正的本·富兰克林。

1453
01:10:30.920 --> 01:10:38.240
He's 99% sure it's not the real Ben Franklin, but he's going to interrogate him anyway.
他有99%的把握确定那不是真正的本·富兰克林，但他还是决定要审问他。

1454
01:10:38.240 --> 01:10:39.880
Yeah, the scene was so funny.
没错，那一幕太搞笑了。

1455
01:10:41.000 --> 01:10:41.880
So funny.
太搞笑了。

1456
01:10:42.080 --> 01:10:47.700
And Dwight is just, like, challenging him with questions about the time period when he lived.
德怀特就像是在用那个时代的问题来挑战他。

1457
01:10:47.900 --> 01:10:53.840
And Andy told us that this was one of his favorite to shoot, and this is what he had to say.
安迪告诉我们这是他最喜欢拍摄的场景之一，他是这么说的。

1458
01:10:53.840 --> 01:10:59.040
This is where my research into Ben Franklin came in handy.
这就是我关于本·富兰克林的研究派上用场的地方。

1459
01:10:59.820 --> 01:11:08.880
There were a bunch of scripted lines in that scene where Rainn Wilson is challenging this Ben Franklin impersonator,
那一幕里有很多剧本台词，雷恩·威尔逊在挑战这位本·富兰克林模仿者，

1460
01:11:09.020 --> 01:11:14.100
trying to trip him up to find the lapse in his knowledge about Ben Franklin.
试图让他露出马脚，找出他对本·富兰克林知识的漏洞。

1461
01:11:14.100 --> 01:11:17.120
And so he's just throwing all these questions.
所以他抛出了所有这些问题。

1462
01:11:17.340 --> 01:11:22.940
But one that he improvised was, are you nearsighted or farsighted?
但他即兴发挥了一个问题：你是近视还是远视？

1463
01:11:23.040 --> 01:11:24.500
That was not in the script.
剧本里并没有这一句。

1464
01:11:24.500 --> 01:11:27.460
It was never discussed beforehand that he was going to say that.
事先完全没讨论过他会说这个。

1465
01:11:27.620 --> 01:11:30.860
He just threw that out in the middle of a take.
他就是在拍摄过程中随口抛出来的。

1466
01:11:30.860 --> 01:11:38.580
And I, because I had just read the Wikipedia page about Ben Franklin, knew that Ben Franklin invented the bifocals.
而我，因为刚读过本·富兰克林的维基百科页面，我知道本·富兰克林发明了双焦眼镜。

1467
01:11:38.580 --> 01:11:47.100
And he invented the bifocals because he needed them, because his distance sight was challenged, as was his reading sight.
他发明双焦眼镜是因为他需要，因为他的远视和近距离阅读视力都有问题。

1468
01:11:47.100 --> 01:11:52.080
And so I was able to say, without having to think about it or hesitate, both.
所以我能够不假思索、毫不犹豫地回答：两者都是。

1469
01:11:52.520 --> 01:11:54.680
That's why I invented the bifocal.
这就是我发明双焦眼镜的原因。

1470
01:11:55.320 --> 01:12:02.060
And that is an unusual, kind of magical, improvised moment.
那是一个不同寻常、近乎神奇的即兴时刻。

1471
01:12:02.060 --> 01:12:09.020
It's so strange that he asked me a question for which I was prepared with the perfect answer.
真奇怪，他问了一个我刚好有完美答案的问题。

1472
01:12:09.260 --> 01:12:10.540
It's very strange.
非常奇怪。

1473
01:12:10.720 --> 01:12:14.340
And in fact, when they called Cut, I remember Mindy Kaling saying,
事实上，当他们喊“卡”的时候，我记得敏迪·卡灵说，

1474
01:12:14.340 --> 01:12:16.080
did you guys work that out beforehand?
你们俩事先商量好了吗？

1475
01:12:16.260 --> 01:12:17.160
And we were both like, no.
我们都说，没有。

1476
01:12:17.320 --> 01:12:19.620
And we were all kind of stumped.
我们当时都有点懵。

1477
01:12:19.920 --> 01:12:22.540
That's, it's very strange that that's an improvised moment.
那确实是一个非常奇妙的即兴时刻。

1478
01:12:23.760 --> 01:12:27.080
And yeah, it ended up in the show, of course, because why, why wouldn't it?
没错，它最终被剪进了剧集里，当然了，为什么不呢？

1479
01:12:28.160 --> 01:12:29.800
So yes, that's my answer.
所以，是的，这就是我的回答。

1480
01:12:30.880 --> 01:12:31.280
Amazing.
太棒了。

1481
01:12:31.460 --> 01:12:35.200
Lady, this is, you know, my nerdy moment where I say it's the group mind.
莱迪，你知道，这是我展现书呆子气的一刻，我要说这就是集体智慧。

1482
01:12:35.580 --> 01:12:38.280
Also, actors, this is why you need to do your prep work.
另外，各位演员，这就是为什么你们需要做准备工作。

1483
01:12:38.460 --> 01:12:39.400
Always, always.
必须的，必须的。

1484
01:12:39.940 --> 01:12:43.940
Guys, actors do not just show up on set and just make it up as they go.
伙计们，演员可不是到了片场才临时发挥的。

1485
01:12:43.940 --> 01:12:44.820
We study.
我们得研究。

1486
01:12:45.060 --> 01:12:45.780
It's a craft.
这是一门手艺。

1487
01:12:46.420 --> 01:12:47.760
We take it seriously.
我们很认真地对待它。

1488
01:12:48.200 --> 01:12:50.740
I always, always try to flesh out my character.
我总是，总是尝试去丰满我的角色。

1489
01:12:50.880 --> 01:12:54.960
And if they've given me any kind of nugget, like, you know, obviously he had Ben Franklin.
如果他们给了我任何一点线索，比如，你知道，显然他有本·富兰克林这个角色。

1490
01:12:55.300 --> 01:12:56.820
I do a deep dive.
我会进行深入挖掘。

1491
01:12:56.960 --> 01:12:59.380
So I have all this in my head in case I need it.
这样我脑子里就有了一切，以备不时之需。

1492
01:13:01.540 --> 01:13:04.880
Lady, do you think that's why we do all these deep dives for the podcast?
莱迪，你觉得这就是我们为播客做所有这些深度挖掘的原因吗？

1493
01:13:05.160 --> 01:13:08.420
Is it like, is it our actor brains at work?
这就像是我们的演员大脑在运作吗？

1494
01:13:08.700 --> 01:13:11.880
Because that's the kind of stuff I would do for a scene.
因为这就是我为一场戏会做的那种准备。

1495
01:13:11.880 --> 01:13:12.320
Yeah.
是的。

1496
01:13:13.480 --> 01:13:20.700
